# Design System Style

## CSS
- Every color, spacing, font size, font weight, line height, radius and shadow is `var(--token)`.
- Use semantic variables only. `--primitive-*` is for `tokens.css` alone.
- Allowed literals: `0`, `1px` borders, `100%`, `auto`, `none`, unitless `1` for flex.
- Class names: `component-name__part` (BEM element style). Variants come from `[data-*]` selectors.
- One CSS file per component, imported at the top of the component file.

```css
/* good */
.budget-card { padding: var(--space-inset-md); color: var(--color-text-default); }
.budget-card[data-status='over'] .budget-card__status { color: var(--color-status-danger); }

/* bad */
.budget-card { padding: 16px; color: #1e293b; }
```

## React / TSX
- Function components with a named export. Props type named `XProps`.
- No `style={{ }}`. Use `className` and `data-*`.
- No `useEffect`, `fetch`, stores or context reads in presentational components.
- No string building for money or dates inside the component. The parent passes `spentLabel="$420"`.
- Semantic HTML first: `<article>`, `<h2>`, `<progress>`, `<button>`. ARIA only where HTML has no answer.
- Every interactive element has an accessible name.

## Tokens JSON
- Primitive names describe the scale: `color.green.600`, `space.4`, `font.size.300`.
- Semantic names describe the job: `color.surface.card`, `space.inset.md`, `font.size.body`.
- Keep layers flat enough to read: three or four path segments.
- Sort keys by scale order, not alphabetically, so the file reads like a ramp.

## Stories
- `title: 'Components/BudgetCard'`. One named export per state (`OnTrack`, `NearLimit`, `OverBudget`).
- Story args use the same display-ready strings as tests.
